{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect adds flow alerts for easier troubleshooting","context":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect has introduced new flow alerts to facilitate faster debugging of MediaConnect flows, sources, and outputs. These alerts are accessible via the MediaConnect API as a text string and the AWS Management Console under the Alerts tab of a flow. The alerts will supplement the existing CloudWatch Metrics and CloudWatch Events for MediaConnect","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/aws-elemental-mediaconnect-flow-alerts-easier-troubleshooting/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect now publishes higher frequency metrics","context":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect has upgraded its metric publishing to Amazon CloudWatch with a higher frequency of 1 second, replacing the previous 1-minute interval. This enhancement offers a near real-time perspective on flow performance, allowing for quicker diagnosis and resolution of issues. The new 1-second metrics can be accessed via the console or CloudWatch API for up to 3 hours after their creation. Existing MediaConnect metrics are now available at the 1-second interval","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/aws-elemental-mediaconnect-publishes-higher-frequency-metrics/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"querying-aws-cloudwatch","skill_description":"Runs SQL queries on CloudWatch Logs data exported as Apache Iceberg tables in S3 Tables. Covers VPC Flow Logs, WAF logs, CloudFront access logs, Route 53 resolver logs, Network Firewall logs, EKS audit logs, Verified Access logs, SES logs, VPC Lattice logs, Step Functions logs, NLB access logs, S3 Server Access Logs, and 20+ other AWS vended data sources. Applies when analyzing network traffic, investigating security incidents, querying exported logs with SQL, enabling S3 Tables integration, configuring log export, correlating logs with other data, running Athena queries on the aws-cloudwatch table bucket, analyzing S3 access patterns, S3 latency investigation, S3 cost attribution, or bucket access auditing.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, s3tables, athena, glue, s3\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, audit, configure\nPersona: developer, data-engineer, devops\nWorkload: data-analytics, observability\n*","skill_name":"querying-aws-cloudwatch"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-investigation","skill_description":"Investigates what is happening in an AWS account from evidence already recorded there. Not for capturing new data from running code (snapshots of function arguments on a live service, Dynamic Instrumentation), questions answered from the CloudWatch Omni context graph or Application Signals service map, or building or changing infrastructure. Covers reading deployment records instead of the newest stored version (completed AppConfig deployments, the version an alias points to, a stack's current template), following a request through every service's own logs (exact per-layer fields, unique failed requests in an alarm's breach window, failure boundary per event), and answering questions from the account's data (exact counts and breakdowns, coverage of the requested range, exact filters and joins, the rule behind failed or unmatched records, verbatim values). Use to triage an alarm, error spike or failed request, trace a request across services, or count, break down, extract or join records.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, appconfig, lambda, cloudformation, dynamodb, s3, athena, glue\nTasks: debug, investigate, query, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: observability, operations","skill_name":"aws-investigation"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region","skill_description":"Enables a multi-region AWS CloudTrail trail with S3 log storage, CloudWatch Logs integration, and CloudWatch Logs Insights queries for security monitoring and compliance auditing. Use when setting up centralized API activity logging across all AWS regions.\n\nServices: cloudtrail, s3, cloudwatch, iam, kms\nTasks: configure, secure, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security, monitoring\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify whether MediaConnect emits CloudWatch Logs or only metrics/alerts"}
